dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5, [dcl.fct]/8: in `decltype(fat(static_cast<A &&>(a)
...))' the k-th element of the expansion names A_k and the k-th function
parameter.  During deduction (substitute_function_type) the parameter pack
`a' was one symbol of the first element's type, and the template map
replaced A by its first element (heterogeneous packs: "type mismatch on
static_cast", f not viable, bin53); during instantiation the type pack was
expanded alone, each element naming `a'.  The function parameter pack is now
bound per element (as for a requires-expression's parameter pack) and
expanded in lockstep with A in both places.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
